<title>GERMANY: Bavarian premier says court could stop EMU.</title>
<headline>Bavarian premier says court could stop EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A leading German Euro-sceptic warned on Thursday that European economic and monetary union (EMU) could be blocked by Germany's Constitutional Court unless the fiscal targets for the single currency were fulfilled.</p>
<p>Bavarian state premier Edmund Stoiber said in an interview with ZDF public television that the court had already ruled that the Maastricht treaty's criteria must be strictly observed or Germany could not take part.</p>
<p>&quot;If the criteria are exceeded and it cannot be prevented politically, then in the end the Constitutional Court will make the final decision,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Stoiber did not go so far as to say that Bavaria would seek to block EMU by going to the Constitutional Court.</p>
</text>
